Test rg35: a block directive may end on the last word of a bank
// 07777 is a usable address -- an ordinary instruction assembles there, and
// bank 0 below puts one at 07777 to prove it. But every directive that
// reserves a BLOCK of words advances cur_pc first and bound-checked the
// result, which is one PAST the last word it used. A block ending exactly at
// 07777 left cur_pc at 010000 and was rejected, so the top word of every bank
// was unreachable to table, text, ascii, type340, variables and constants.
//
// Each bank below ends its block exactly on 07777. Every one of these was
// rejected before 09-Sep-2026; if the check ever goes back to testing the pc
// after the block instead of the last address in it, they fail again.
//
// The .ref pins the words, so it also catches a "fix" that let the block
// through by silently dropping its last word.

bank 0
100/
beg,    hlt
07777/
        lac beg         // an ordinary instruction reaches the ceiling

bank 1
07770/
        table 010, 0123 // 8 words, 07770 through 07777

bank 2
07777/
        text "a"

bank 3
07777/
        ascii "a"

bank 4
07777/
        type340 "a"

bank 5
07777/
lbl,    text "b"        // the labelTrailer form takes a different rule

bank 6
        var topvar
100/
        dio topvar
07777/
        variables       // the implicit block, placed by setVarsPC

bank 7
100/
        lac [0123]
07777/
        constants       // the implicit block, placed by setConstPC

start beg:0
